# What Prettier must not touch.
#
# This file is the whole of the format gate's scope: `npm run format:check`
# runs Prettier over the repository root, so a path is formatted unless it is
# excluded here or Prettier has no parser for it (Rust, shell and TOML fall in
# the second group and need no entry).
#
# Three kinds of thing are excluded, and nothing else should be:
#
#   1. Generated or vendored output, which no human edits.
#   2. Files another gate already owns, so two tools never disagree about the
#      same file.
#   3. Prose, which markdownlint and cspell own.

# --- Generated or vendored -------------------------------------------------

node_modules/
dist/
target/
# Astro's build cache. It appears only once the documentation site has been
# built, so a checkout that has never run it sees nothing here.
apps/docs/.astro/
# npm writes this file and its formatting is npm's own; reformatting it makes
# the next `npm install` rewrite it back.
package-lock.json
# ESLint writes the lint ratchet's baseline (`npm run lint:baseline`,
# `npm run lint:prune`) in its own formatting, and rewrites it on every prune.
/eslint-suppressions.json
# The environments uv builds for the Python projects, each kept out of git by an
# ignore file of its own inside the folder, which Prettier does not read.
.venv/
# Build output a tool writes under a directory of that name.
build/
# Scratch work, which nobody formats.
/tmp/
# Copier writes the answers file on every render and update, in its own
# formatting.
.copier-answers.yml

# --- Owned by another gate -------------------------------------------------

# The design documentation. markdownlint (`.markdownlint-cli2.yaml`) and cspell
# (`cspell.json`) are its gates, and it is the source of truth for the project;
# no formatter rewrites it.
apps/docs/src/content/docs/

# The Kubernetes manifests. `ci/gates/k8s-manifests.py` renders every
# overlay and asserts on the result, and kustomize's own conventions (field
# order, document splits) govern how they are written.
deployments/k8s/

# --- Prose -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Markdown style is markdownlint's; a second formatter with its own opinion
# about line wrapping and list markers would fight it on every file.
*.md
*.mdx

# --- The project's own -----------------------------------------------------

